SELECT 'WSQ CompTIA Server+ Training Singapore: SK0-005 Exam Domains, Funding and Pearson VUE Testing', 'wsq-comptia-server-plus-training-singapore-guide', 'CompTIA Server+ is vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited and recognised by employers worldwide. This guide breaks down every SK0-005 exam domain and weighting, explains what the certification is actually worth in the Singapore job market, and sets out the WSQ funding - up to 70% subsidy, or up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above - that brings the fee down. Train with an Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner and sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.',
       '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA Server+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>SK0-005</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA Server+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>Server+ is the only major server certification with no vendor lock-in and, uniquely in the CompTIA portfolio, it does not expire - the SK0-005 credential is issued for life. For data centre and infrastructure roles it covers the hardware, virtualisation, storage and disaster recovery ground that OS-specific certifications skip.</p><h2>The SK0-005 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA Server+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>SK0-005</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / server administration</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Does not expire - Server+ is a lifetime certification for exams taken from SK0-005 onwards</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends A+ plus around two years of hands-on server or data centre experience. Not enforced.</p><h2>SK0-005 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Server Hardware Installation and Management</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Server form factors and components, rack installation and power, storage technologies and RAID levels, and hardware maintenance and lifecycle.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Server Administration</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>The largest domain: installing and configuring server operating systems, virtualisation and cloud integration, licensing, asset management, documentation and change control.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Disaster Recovery</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Physical and logical server security, data security and encryption, hardening, backup methodologies, replication and disaster recovery planning.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Troubleshooting</strong></td><td>28%</td><td>Applying a structured methodology to hardware, OS, storage, network and security faults, including boot and performance problems.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified Server+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the SK0-005 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Server Administrator, Systems Administrator, Data Centre Technician, Infrastructure Engineer, Network Administrator.</p><h2>Train and sit your exam in one place</h2><p>Two accreditations matter here, and we hold both.</p><blockquote><p><strong>We are an Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner.</strong> Our trainers and courseware are approved by CompTIA to deliver CompTIA Server+ training, so what you are taught is aligned to the current published exam objectives rather than to an outdated third-party syllabus.</p><p><strong>We are a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center.</strong> CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network, and our centre is one of them. You can register and sit your proctored SK0-005 exam at our training centre - the same room you studied in.</p></blockquote><p>That combination removes the most common friction point after training: booking a test slot somewhere unfamiliar, weeks after the course, once the material has gone cold. Sitting the exam where you trained, while the labs are still fresh, measurably improves your odds.</p><p>Note that the course fee <strong>does not include the exam voucher</strong>. Vouchers are purchased separately, and we offer CompTIA exam vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore. Ask us when you enrol.</p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA Server+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024048318</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024048318" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024048318.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024048318" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the SK0-005 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The SK0-005 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored SK0-005 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends A+ plus around two years of hands-on server or data centre experience. Not enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Does not expire - Server+ is a lifetime certification for exams taken from SK0-005 onwards</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA Server+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified Server+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>',
       'https://pub-77c0dec029944b0386e40673ce81081f.r2.dev/blog/auto-20260823-192650-comptia-server-sk0-005-certification-a-lifetime-credential.png',
       'Tertiary Infotech Academy', 1, '2025-10-21',
       'TGS-2024048318', 'TGS-2024048318',
       'WSQ CompTIA Server+ Training Singapore | SK0-005 Guide', 'SK0-005 exam domains, weightings and funding for WSQ CompTIA Server+ training in Singapore. Up to 70% course fee funding (90% for age 40+). Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner and Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center.', 'comptia server+ singapore, comptia server+ training, comptia server+ certification, sk0-005 exam, sk0-005 exam domains, wsq comptia server+, comptia training singapore, comptia certification singapore, skillsfuture comptia course, pearson vue test center singapore, comptia authorised delivery partner, comptia server+ course fee funding',
       115, '2025-10-21 09:00:00', '2025-10-21 09:00:00'
FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS
  (SELECT 1 FROM (SELECT post_id FROM mmd_blog_post WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-server-plus-training-singapore-guide') x);

